$DIR/test.p:6:22: invalid argument: x (variable of type int) is not a pointer
    This error occurs when unsafe.Slice is called with a pointer argument that
    is not of pointer type or a length argument that is not of integer type,
    negative, or out of bounds. It also occurs if it is used in a package
    compiled for a language version before go1.17.
    (see "Package unsafe" in the Plutonium spec, section 20.1)
    (run "pluto explain E0134" for a longer explanation)
